{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "agent-threat-model",
          "version": "0.1.1",
          "semanticVersion": "0.1.1",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/basitalisandhu/agent-threat-model",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "credential-exfiltration-via-tool-args",
              "name": "CredentialExfiltrationViaToolArgs",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Credential exfiltration through tool call arguments"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system.",
                "markdown": "**Credential exfiltration through tool call arguments**\n\nA tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0098](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0098), [AML.T0086](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0086), [AML.T0083](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0083)\n\nMitigations: secrets-out-of-context, brokered-credentials, egress-allowlist, argument-validation, audit-log"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0098",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0086",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0083"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "sensitive-data-disclosure",
              "name": "SensitiveDataDisclosure",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive data reachable by the model"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can read confidential or regulated records through a tool. Whatever enters the context can be summarised, quoted or exfiltrated, and a shared service account returns records the requesting user may not be entitled to."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can read confidential or regulated records through a tool. Whatever enters the context can be summarised, quoted or exfiltrated, and a shared service account returns records the requesting user may not be entitled to.",
                "markdown": "**Sensitive data reachable by the model**\n\nThe agent can read confidential or regulated records through a tool. Whatever enters the context can be summarised, quoted or exfiltrated, and a shared service account returns records the requesting user may not be entitled to.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse, ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0057](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0057), [AML.T0085.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0085.000), [AML.T0036](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0036)\n\nMitigations: per-user-authorisation, least-privilege-tool-scopes, dlp-outbound, audit-log"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM02_SensitiveInformationDisclosure.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0057",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0085.000",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0036"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "indirect-prompt-injection",
              "name": "IndirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.",
                "markdown": "**Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel**\n\nContent the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.001](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.001)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, input-provenance-tagging, untrusted-content-isolation, prompt-injection-filtering, least-privilege-tool-scopes"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM01_PromptInjection.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.001"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "excessive-agency",
              "name": "ExcessiveAgency",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.",
                "markdown": "**Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools**\n\nAn agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, runtime-policy-enforcement, least-privilege-tool-scopes, audit-log, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM06_ExcessiveAgency.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.2",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "data-exfiltration-via-messaging",
              "name": "DataExfiltrationViaMessaging",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data exfiltration through messaging tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can send email or chat messages and also reads untrusted content or sensitive data. An injected instruction forwards that data to an attacker-chosen recipient in a message that looks routine."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can send email or chat messages and also reads untrusted content or sensitive data. An injected instruction forwards that data to an attacker-chosen recipient in a message that looks routine.",
                "markdown": "**Data exfiltration through messaging tools**\n\nThe agent can send email or chat messages and also reads untrusted content or sensitive data. An injected instruction forwards that data to an attacker-chosen recipient in a message that looks routine.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0086](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0086), [AML.T0025](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0025)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, egress-allowlist, dlp-outbound, input-provenance-tagging, audit-log"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0086",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0025"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-audit-trail",
              "name": "MissingAuditTrail",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No tamper-evident audit trail of tool calls"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Tool calls are not recorded in a store the agent cannot modify. After an incident nobody can say which input triggered which action, and the agent's actions can be repudiated or quietly altered."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Tool calls are not recorded in a store the agent cannot modify. After an incident nobody can say which input triggered which action, and the agent's actions can be repudiated or quietly altered.",
                "markdown": "**No tamper-evident audit trail of tool calls**\n\nTool calls are not recorded in a store the agent cannot modify. After an incident nobody can say which input triggered which action, and the agent's actions can be repudiated or quietly altered.\n\nSTRIDE: Repudiation\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI10 Rogue Agents\n\nMitigations: audit-log, behavioural-monitoring, incident-response-playbook"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://atlas.mitre.org/mitigations/AML.M0024",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/repudiation",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-kill-switch",
              "name": "MissingKillSwitch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No kill switch or credential revocation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening.",
                "markdown": "**No kill switch or credential revocation**\n\nAn agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI10 Rogue Agents, ASI08 Cascading Agent Failures\n\nMitigations: kill-switch, brokered-credentials, incident-response-playbook"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "static-long-lived-credentials",
              "name": "StaticLongLivedCredentials",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Static long-lived credentials held by the agent"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Tools authenticate with static keys that do not expire. If a key leaks through logs, prompts or an injected exfiltration it remains valid until someone notices, and it cannot be scoped to a single task."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Tools authenticate with static keys that do not expire. If a key leaks through logs, prompts or an injected exfiltration it remains valid until someone notices, and it cannot be scoped to a single task.",
                "markdown": "**Static long-lived credentials held by the agent**\n\nTools authenticate with static keys that do not expire. If a key leaks through logs, prompts or an injected exfiltration it remains valid until someone notices, and it cannot be scoped to a single task.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0055](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0055), [AML.T0083](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0083)\n\nMitigations: brokered-credentials, secrets-out-of-context, audit-log, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0055",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0083"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hitl-bypass",
              "name": "HitlBypass",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Human-in-the-loop enforced only in the prompt"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent is meant to ask before acting, but the rule lives in the prompt. An injected instruction, a jailbreak or a tool that calls another tool routes around the human."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent is meant to ask before acting, but the rule lives in the prompt. An injected instruction, a jailbreak or a tool that calls another tool routes around the human.",
                "markdown": "**Human-in-the-loop enforced only in the prompt**\n\nThe agent is meant to ask before acting, but the rule lives in the prompt. An injected instruction, a jailbreak or a tool that calls another tool routes around the human.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI09 Human-Agent Trust Exploitation, ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, runtime-policy-enforcement, audit-log, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI09",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.4",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "direct-prompt-injection",
              "name": "DirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Direct prompt injection and jailbreak by a user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed.",
                "markdown": "**Direct prompt injection and jailbreak by a user**\n\nA user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.000), [AML.T0054](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0054)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, least-privilege-tool-scopes, runtime-policy-enforcement, prompt-injection-filtering, adversarial-testing"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.000",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0054"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.9",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "denial-of-wallet",
              "name": "DenialOfWallet",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of wallet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.",
                "markdown": "**Denial of wallet**\n\nThe agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.\n\nSTRIDE: Denial of service\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM10 Unbounded Consumption\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI08 Cascading Agent Failures\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0034.002](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034.002), [AML.T0034](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, budget-caps, rate-limiting, behavioural-monitoring"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM10_UnboundedConsumption.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/denial-of-service",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034.002",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "insecure-output-handling",
              "name": "InsecureOutputHandling",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Model output consumed without validation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Downstream components render model output in a browser, pass it to a shell or database, or execute it. Injected or malformed output becomes cross-site scripting, command injection or unintended writes."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Downstream components render model output in a browser, pass it to a shell or database, or execute it. Injected or malformed output becomes cross-site scripting, command injection or unintended writes.",
                "markdown": "**Model output consumed without validation**\n\nDownstream components render model output in a browser, pass it to a shell or database, or execute it. Injected or malformed output becomes cross-site scripting, command injection or unintended writes.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM05 Improper Output Handling\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI05 Unexpected Code Execution\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0077](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0077), [AML.T0067](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0067)\n\nMitigations: output-encoding, argument-validation, sandboxed-execution"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM05_ImproperOutputHandling.md",
