              "id": "agent-config-tampering",
              "name": "AgentConfigTampering",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Agent configuration tampering"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Prompts, tool lists and policies live in files or stores an agent can write to, or that lack change control. Modifying them silently changes what the agent is allowed to do."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Prompts, tool lists and policies live in files or stores an agent can write to, or that lack change control. Modifying them silently changes what the agent is allowed to do.",
                "markdown": "**Agent configuration tampering**\n\nPrompts, tool lists and policies live in files or stores an agent can write to, or that lack change control. Modifying them silently changes what the agent is allowed to do.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM03 Supply Chain, LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI10 Rogue Agents, ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0081](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0081)\n\nMitigations: runtime-policy-enforcement, tool-integrity-pinning, audit-log, least-privilege-tool-scopes"
